BrainChip Connect is a React Native app. The repository ships the app's own
source, its native Android and iOS projects, and a small number of files that
came from elsewhere or carry their own terms; those are listed first. Every
library the app is built from is fetched at build time and is not
redistributed by this repository; those are listed afterwards, and each keeps
its own terms.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Patches to third-party packages
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`patches/` holds two patch-package patches. `npm ci` applies them to the
installed copies of the packages named below (`package.json` line 10,
`"postinstall": "patch-package"`). Each patch is a change to that package's
own source and is offered under that package's licence, not this
repository's.

  patches/react-native-ble-plx+3.5.0.patch
    Package:   react-native-ble-plx 3.5.0
    Upstream:  https://github.com/dotintent/react-native-ble-plx
    Changes:   android/src/main/java/com/bleplx/utils/SafePromise.java, so a
               promise is never rejected with a null or empty error code.
    Licence:   Apache License, Version 2.0, as the package's LICENSE file
               states: "Copyright 2016 Polidea, Copyright 2021 intent
               sp. z o.o." The package's package.json declares "MIT" in
               its license field instead; both statements are the package's
               own and are recorded here as found.

  patches/react-native-screens+4.27.0.patch
    Package:   react-native-screens 4.27.0
    Upstream:  https://github.com/software-mansion/react-native-screens
    Changes:   type-only edits under src/fabric/ so React Native 0.83's
               codegen accepts the native command signatures.
    Licence:   MIT License. Copyright (c) 2018 Software Mansion.

`ios/Podfile` lines 35 to 49 rewrite one line of `Pods/fmt/include/fmt/base.h`
after `pod install`, so the {fmt} library builds with the Apple Clang that
ships with Xcode 26. {fmt} (https://github.com/fmtlib/fmt) is fetched by
CocoaPods through React Native's `fmt.podspec` and is not redistributed here;
its licence is the MIT-style licence in its own repository.

