--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Key material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Path:      android/app/debug.keystore

This is the Android debug signing key that every React Native project and
Android toolchain ships, byte-for-byte identical to the copy in the React
Native template. Its password is `android` and its alias is
`androiddebugkey`, as `android/app/build.gradle` lines 112 to 115 spell out,
and its self-signed certificate names "CN=Android Debug, OU=Android,
O=Unknown, C=US", created on 31 December 2013. It signs development builds only and protects nothing.

No release signing key, upload key, service account or API key is in this
repository. The release build reads its keystore from the environment
(`android/app/build.gradle`), and `.gitignore` refuses `*.keystore` and
`*.jks` apart from this one file.

